  "rules": [
    "PairingOffer is Borsh {version: u8 = 1, hrp: String (\"salt\" | \"tsalt\" | \"dsalt\"), genesis: [u8;8] the first 8 bytes of the genesis hash, key: [u8;32] the server key (a valid Ed25519 key, not of small order), nonce: [u8;16] random, slug: Option<String> (3-32 of [a-z0-9-], not starting with '-'), name: String (at most 32 characters, none of Unicode Cc, Cf, U+2028, U+2029; may be empty), created_at: u64 Unix ms, expires_at: u64 Unix ms with created_at < expires_at <= created_at + 30 minutes}; nothing in it is secret or signed; a reader refuses trailing bytes",
    "link = \"salt:grain-pair?o=\" base64url without padding of Borsh(PairingOffer); white space around it is allowed; padding, spare bits, any other character or a further parameter is refused",
    "code = the first 4 bytes of BLAKE3-derive_key(\"Saltix grain pairing code v1\", Borsh(PairingOffer)) as a big-endian u32, modulo 1 000 000; code_text is its 6 digits with leading zeros in two groups of 3 separated by one space",
    "fingerprint(key) = the first 4 bytes of the key in lower-case hex; server_address = the key's personal address (kind 0) on the offer's network",
    "a wallet on a chain takes an offer at now when it is of form, hrp is the chain's prefix and genesis its first 8 bytes (other_network), created_at <= now + 5 minutes (ahead), and now < expires_at (expired), checked in that order",
    "pairing frame plaintext = \"SGP1\" ‖ Borsh(PairFrame), sealed as grain frames are and kept in the mailbox; PairFrame = 0 Request(PairRequest {offer: [u8;16] the offer's nonce, slug: String, owner: [u8;32] account}) from the owner's grain alias to the offer key's personal address | 1 Answer(PairAnswer {offer: [u8;16], slug: String, owner: [u8;32], result: u8, proof: Option<[u8;64]>}) back; a reader refuses another magic (not_pairing), trailing bytes, an unknown tag or result, a slug that names no grain, and a proof present when result is not 0 or missing when it is",
    "results: 0 accepted (proof = ServerKeyProof.proof: Ed25519 by the offer's key over BLAKE3-derive_key(\"Saltix grain server v1\", Borsh((genesis_hash [32], slug, owner [32])))), 1 used, 2 expired, 3 unknown, 4 other_app, 5 not_owner",
    "the computer judges in order: request.offer is not the offer's nonce → 3; answered already → 0 again for the same slug and owner (even past the expiry), else 1; now >= expires_at → 2; the offer names a slug and the request another → 4; the registry holds the slug for another account, or retired → 5; else 0, and it keeps (slug, owner) as the offer's answer",
    "the wallet takes an answer only for its request in flight: the same offer nonce, slug and owner (mismatch), and an accepted one only with a proof that verifies under the offer's key for that slug and owner on its chain (proof); it waits at most 2 minutes"
  ],
